        "original_id": "bd194ae9-05fb-5ed1-8f91-0dfebd6c513d",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Nivek Ogre, Frank Sinatra, Kevin Crompton, Dave Ogilvie\n- Organizations: Skinny Puppy\n- Roles: musician, performance artist, actor, singer, producer\n- Products: The Voice of Frank Sinatra, From Here to Eternity\n- Concepts: stage names and aliases\n\nFacts:\n- Frank Sinatra was born on December 12, 1915, and became an American singer, actor, and producer who was one of the most popular and influential musical artists of the 20th century.\n- Frank Sinatra released his debut album, \"The Voice of Frank Sinatra\", in 1946.\n- Frank Sinatra's career was revived in 1953 by the success of \"From Here to Eternity\", and his performance won an Academy Award and a Golden Globe Award for Best Supporting Actor.\n- Nivek Ogre was born Kevin Graham Ogilvie on December 5, 1962, and is a Canadian musician, performance artist, and actor.\n- Nivek Ogre is best known as a founding member of the industrial music group Skinny Puppy.\n- Nivek Ogre used his alias partly for practical reasons because Skinny Puppy already included Kevin Crompton, also known as cEvin Key, and was produced by Dave Ogilvie, also known as Rave.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
